<%# What a card looks like everywhere its script can't run: email, feeds, the writer's
    plain-text excerpt, an RSS reader. Rendering it here is what spares every one of those
    from having to know cards exist.

    The modifier class is load-bearing, not decoration. Lexxy inserts a card inline, so the
    editor leaves it inside a <p> — and a <div> inside a <p> is not something an HTML parser
    will keep there. Re-parsing the rendered body hoists this wrapper out of the paragraph
    and out of the attachment it belongs to, which left HtmlCard.expand replacing an
    attachment that no longer owned its own skeleton, and the post showed the card twice.
    expand clears these first for that reason. %>
<div class="kg-card kg-html-card kg-html-card--static"><%= html_card.static_html %></div>
